            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "This still reproduces on nightly (`NVIM v0.13.0-dev-1825+g402a494f47`) and on v0.12.5. Here's a repro that fails every time with `nvim --clean`, plus why the stale `foldinfos` entry exists.\n\nSave as `repro.lua`, then run `nvim --clean` and `:luafile repro.lua`. `OptionSet` doesn't fire during startup, so `-c 'luafile repro.lua'` won't show it.\n\n```lua\nvim.o.foldmethod = \"expr\"\nvim.o.foldexpr = \"v:lua.vim.treesitter.foldexpr()\"\n\n-- A buffer with no tree-sitter parser.\nlocal buf = vim.api.nvim_create_buf(true, true)\nvim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(buf, 0, -1, false, { \"a\", \"b\" })\nvim.api.nvim_set_current_buf(buf)\nvim.fn.foldlevel(1) -- evaluates foldexpr, creating fold state for buf\nvim.cmd.enew()\n\n-- Wipe it from inside an autocmd callback.\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"User\", {\n  pattern = \"Wipe\",\n  once = true,\n  callback = function()\n    vim.api.nvim_buf_delete(buf, { force = true })\n  end,\n})\nvim.api.nvim_exec_autocmds(\"User\", { pattern = \"Wipe\" })\n\nvim.cmd(\"set foldminlines=1\")\n```\n\n```\nOptionSet Autocommands for \"foldminlines\": ... runtime/lua/vim/treesitter.lua:89: Invalid buffer id: 2\nstack traceback:\n\t[C]: in function '__index'\n\t.../runtime/lua/vim/treesitter.lua:89: in function 'get_parser'\n\t.../runtime/lua/vim/treesitter/_fold.lua:35: in function 'new'\n\t.../runtime/lua/vim/treesitter/_fold.lua:449: in function <.../runtime/lua/vim/treesitter/_fold.lua:443>\n```\n\n**Why the entry goes stale:** `foldexpr()` relies on two things to clear `foldinfos[bufnr]`. One is a buffer-local `{ BufUnload, VimEnter, FileType }` autocmd. The other is the parser's `on_detach`.\n\nA buffer with no parser has no `on_detach`. If it's wiped from inside another autocmd callback, `BufUnload` doesn't run because autocmds don't nest, and the autocmd is deleted along with the buffer. The entry is never removed, so every later global `foldminlines`/`foldnestmax` change hits it again.\n\nIn practice this happens with [codediff.nvim](https://github.com/esmuellert/codediff.nvim). Its diff buffers have no filetype and `bufhidden=wipe`, and its compact view sets `foldminlines` on each refresh.\n\nThe `nvim_buf_is_valid()` check suggested above would stop the crash. Clearing the entry on detach also keeps stale entries from building up, since `on_detach` fires however the buffer is wiped. I patched nightly's `_fold.lua` and the repro stopped failing:\n\n```lua\n    nvim_on({ 'BufUnload', 'VimEnter', 'FileType' }, nil, { buf = bufnr, once = true }, function()\n      foldinfos[bufnr] = nil\n    end)\n    api.nvim_buf_attach(bufnr, false, {\n      on_detach = function()\n        foldinfos[bufnr] = nil\n      end,\n    })\n```\n",
